{
  "$comment": "Message grouping, row presentation and date pills (docs/design/message-surface-and-meta.md C4). Read by the four kit tests through each kit's messageGroupPosition / messageRowPresentation (and Vue's flareTimelineRows) pure functions. Messages carry their surface (spec/message-surface-vectors.json): recall, delete and system notices are centered. Times are UTC instants; tests pin utcOffsetMinutes and nowMs. Change the rules and the cases together.",
  "version": 1,
  "timeGapMs": 300000,
  "nowMs": 1792634400000,
  "utcOffsetMinutes": 480,
  "rules": {
    "shareGroup": "Two neighbouring messages share a run when both have the same non-empty senderId, |atMs difference| <= timeGapMs, neither is centered, and both are cards or neither is (bubble and bareMedia mix; a switch between card and the others breaks the run).",
    "breaks": "A date pill or the unread divider between two messages also ends the run: the message before it closes its run, the one after it opens a new run.",
    "position": "single (no neighbour in its run), first, middle, last. Centered rows are always single.",
    "presentation": "edge = position single or first. Incoming: showAvatar = showIncomingAvatar (default true) and edge; reserveAvatarSpace = showIncomingAvatar; showSenderName = group conversation and showGroupSenderName (default true) and edge; avatarPlacement leading. Own messages: showAvatar = showSelfAvatar (default false) and edge; reserveAvatarSpace = showSelfAvatar; showSenderName false; avatarPlacement trailing. Single chats keep showing the peer's avatar. Centered rows: no avatar, no name, no gutter, no tail.",
    "tail": "Only a bubble surface draws a tail, on the last message of its run (single or last). bareMedia and card never do; a card uses radius.lg corners.",
    "datePill": "Before the first message and wherever the local calendar day changes. Labels: today and yesterday (the kit's own today / yesterday strings), monthDay (month and day in the locale's form, same year as now), yearMonthDay (with the year). No time-of-day separators: every message carries its own clock. The pill's background must differ from the timeline canvas.",
    "unread": "The unread divider sits right before unreadFromId (after that day's date pill when both fall there). Its count is the number of messages from it to the end not sent by the viewer.",
    "clock": "The time on a message is the clock only (no date prefix), in the kit / app locale (never the device's): HH:mm in 24-hour locales, h:mm a in 12-hour ones."
  },
